# The generated stylesheets are compared byte for byte with what the build writes, and the build writes LF. Without
# this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf) gets CRLF and the package's up-to-date test fails on an unchanged file. The
# parts of base.css are kept LF too, so that a part and the generated file show the same text.
css/**/*.css text eol=lf
# The vendored fonts are binary, whatever a heuristic thinks.
fonts/**/*.woff2 binary
# The compiled theme module is compared byte for byte too, and TypeScript writes LF (tsconfig.theme.json).
js/** text eol=lf
# Its source is LF too: the boot script is a template literal, and takes the line ends of the file it is written in.
src/theme.ts text eol=lf
